  - title: How do I say it?
    number: 8
    heartsNeeded: 8
    path: 0
    conditions:
      days: 0
      seasons: 0
      dayFrom: 0
      dayTo: 0
      minYear: 0
      minTotalDays: 0
      weather: 0
      requireFlags: []
      anyFlags: []
      forbidFlags: []
      counters: []
    pages:
    - Everybody says I should talk to Walt. Kenji says it. Frank says it. Eleni would have said it, loudly.
    - I could go round there and say it to his face. All of it. The hospital, the money, thirty years of being too proud.
    - Or... his fence. His fence has been crooked for twenty years and I've told him every single afternoon. I could just go and fix it. He'd know what it meant.
    - Words or a fence. Which?
    happy: 0
    ask:
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      minQuality: 0
      questTitle: 
      questText: 
      reminder: []
      thanks: []
    choice:
      enabled: 1
      optionA: Say it to his face
      replyA:
      - Words, then. Out loud. Like a grown man.
      - I'll go tomorrow. If I'm not back by lunch, he's hit me with a level.
      flagsA:
      - gus_walt_talked
      optionB: Fix his fence instead
      replyB:
      - The fence. Yes. He'll understand the fence.
      - Twenty posts. Straight as a rule. And I won't say a single word while I do it. That'll be the hardest part.
      flagsB:
      - gus_fixed_fence
    setFlags: []
    reward:
      gold: 0
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      friendship: 0
  - title: Tea on the porch
    number: 9
    heartsNeeded: 9
    path: 1
    conditions:
      days: 0
      seasons: 0
      dayFrom: 0
      dayTo: 0
      minYear: 0
      minTotalDays: 0
      weather: 0
      requireFlags: []
      anyFlags: []
      forbidFlags: []
      counters: []
    pages:
    - I said it. All of it. On his porch, with Rosa listening through the window and pretending to dust.
    - He didn't say anything for a long time. Then he said, 'You should have told me, you old goat. I'd have lent you the money.'
    - We didn't have the money, either of us. That's the stupid part. We sat there and drank tea until it was dark.
    happy: 0
    ask:
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      minQuality: 0
      questTitle: 
      questText: 
      reminder: []
      thanks: []
    choice:
      enabled: 0
